## 📦 Product Overview

### Problem Summary
Small businesses, freelancers, and bookkeepers spend 10-20 hours per month manually typing invoice data from PDF invoices into Excel or accounting software. This is tedious, error-prone, and expensive work that costs $250-500/month in labor. Existing solutions are either too expensive (enterprise tools) or too generic (general PDF processors).

### Product Description
InvoiceExtractor is a focused SaaS tool that allows users to:
- Upload invoice PDFs (digital or scanned)
- Auto-extract vendor, date, amount, and line items
- Review and correct extracted data in user-friendly interface
- Create vendor templates for repeat suppliers
- Export accounting-ready CSV/Excel files
- Simple subscription model: $20/month saves $400/month in labor

---

## 🔧 Suggested Tech Stack (Free/Low-Cost)

- **Frontend**: React.js + TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, hosted on Vercel (free)
- **Backend**: Node.js + Express, hosted on Railway (free tier)
- **Database**: PostgreSQL on Supabase (free tier)
- **PDF Processing**: pdf-parse for digital PDFs, Tesseract.js for OCR
- **Payments**: Stripe for subscription billing
- **Email**: EmailJS or Resend (free tier)

---

## 🥅 MVP Scope (Invoice-Focused)

- Upload single invoice PDF (up to 10MB)
- Extract vendor name, invoice number, date, total amount
- Extract line items (description, quantity, price, total)
- Manual correction interface for all fields
- Export to CSV/Excel with accounting columns
- Save vendor templates for repeat suppliers
- Simple subscription model (free: 5 invoices, pro: $20 for 100 invoices)

